card.statement:
(<<cite:Dutkay2014>>) A quadrature mirror filter (QMF) for $r$ is a function $m_0$ in $L^{\infty}(Y,\mu)$ with the property

\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{r(\omega)=z} |m_0(\omega)|^2=1,z\in Y.
\end{equation}

A QMF basis is a set of $n$ QMF's $m_0,m_1,\ldots,m_{n-1}$ such that

\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{r(\omega)=z} m_i(\omega)\overline{m_j}(\omega)=1\delta_{ij},\,i,j\in \{0,1,\ldots,n-1\},z\in Y.
\end{equation}
